WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:04.850
Rather than seeing the world in the immediate
aftermath of Thanos' attack, Avengers 4 might

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:09.190
take us back to the Marvel Cinematic Universe
five years into the new status quo.

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:11.099
Is the latest rumor true?

00:00:11.099 --> 00:00:12.179
Let's break down the possibilities.

00:00:12.179 --> 00:00:13.240
Big casting clues

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:17.720
One possible confirmation of the five-year
time jump rumor comes thanks to the movie's

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:18.720
casting.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:23.020
While Scott Lang's daughter, Cassie, has been
played thus far by Abby Ryder Fortson in the

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:28.380
two Ant-Man films, the superhero daughter
could be growing up fast suspiciously fast.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:32.770
In April 2018, just before the release of
Infinity War, news leaked that Marvel had

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:36.590
cast a new actress, Emma Fuhrmann, as Cassie
for Avengers 4.

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:41.730
On its own, this isn't huge news the MCU has
recast roles before but Fuhrmann happens to

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:45.020
be seven years older than her predecessor
in the role.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:50.230
That's a big jump, all-but-confirming that
this story plans on aging Cassie, quickly.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:54.350
It's a fairly abrupt shift, considering the
younger actress just played the role in Ant-Man

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:57.829
and the Wasp, which takes place during the
events of Infinity War.

00:00:57.829 --> 00:01:02.149
If the sequel starts where Avengers 3 left
off, then why would they need such an older

00:01:02.149 --> 00:01:03.149
performer?

00:01:03.149 --> 00:01:04.860
Add in a time jump, and it all makes sense.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:05.860
A Thanos... paradise?

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:09.280
So what would a five-year gap between the
two Avengers sequels mean for the story?

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:13.720
For one thing, we'd get a serious look at
how people have adjusted to half of the universe

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:14.920
being gone.

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:19.460
While grief can last for a lifetime, five
years is a long time to get over some initial

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:20.460
shock.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:24.610
This way, we'd actually see the lasting effects
of the Avengers' devastating loss.

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:29.110
Lots of rumors about the movie revolve around
beating Thanos with time travel, which sounds

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:30.310
like the smart move.

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:34.690
But what would the ethical implications be
of erasing years of experience from the Infinity

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:38.090
War's survivors, years after the universe
has begun to move on?

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:41.080
It could throw a wrench into the Avengers'
plans for fixing things.

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:42.080
The story of Stark

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:46.460
Aside from Thanos himself, the most important
character in Infinity War is arguably Tony

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:47.460
Stark.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:50.600
The movie begins with him and Pepper talking
about the future, thinking about having a

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:53.049
child and contemplating retirement.

00:01:53.049 --> 00:01:56.979
But retirement looks a lot different when
your last battle ends in your biggest loss.

00:01:56.979 --> 00:02:01.100
We don't know if Pepper survived the snap,
but if she did, it's possible that the couple

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:04.369
could have moved on from Infinity War by having
a child.

00:02:04.369 --> 00:02:09.119
If the movie starts five years after the war,
then Tony would face a devastating decision

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:11.730
what if saving the universe meant giving up
his kid?

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:15.900
Would he really sacrifice his own flesh and
blood just to pal around with Peter Parker

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:16.900
again?

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:18.030
Well, Aunt May, maybe.

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:19.030
But Pete?

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:20.030
Battle of New York Part II

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:22.700
While we really don't know where Avengers
4 is going, there have been enough set leaks

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:24.040
to give us some huge clues.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:29.010
For months, we've seen photos of the production
apparently shooting a new version of The Avengers'

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:34.180
climactic Battle of New York, with old costumes
and hairstyles on set further affirming that

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:35.870
we've seen some of this before.

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:37.340
How they do it, we don't know.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:42.150
But unless Marvel is playing eleven-dimensional
chess and leaking monumental misdirection,

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:44.150
it's almost definitely going to happen.

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:48.430
The idea of a five-year time jump adds some
fuel to the time travel argument.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:52.920
After all, if the movie involves time travel,
then who cares what time it is when the story

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:53.920
starts?

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:57.489
It could be five years into the future or
fifty years, and all still end happily on

00:02:57.489 --> 00:02:59.880
the same day the Infinity War started.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:02.160
Think Back to the Future, think Terminator.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:06.540
As soon as going back in time is on the table,
all the problems of a time jump can be undone

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:07.540
just like that.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:08.540
The sidelined Avenger

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:12.359
After sitting out Infinity War, Avengers 4
will finally see the return of Clint Barton

00:03:12.359 --> 00:03:14.830
— but not necessarily Hawkeye.

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:19.769
At this point, it's all but certain that Jeremy
Renner will be coming back as Ronin, a samurai-inspired

00:03:19.769 --> 00:03:24.379
character whose mantle has been taken up by
quite a few people in the comics including

00:03:24.379 --> 00:03:25.379
Hawkeye.

00:03:25.379 --> 00:03:29.310
Hawkeye sat out Infinity War while living
under house arrest with his loving family

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:31.300
following the events of Civil War.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.989
But what if Thanos' attack destroyed his family?

00:03:33.989 --> 00:03:35.830
Would the snap make Hawkeye snap?

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:36.830
We think so.

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:38.720
And we think it's going to be awesome.

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:42.890
A five-year gap and a family in the fridge
would provide a perfect cover for the development

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:46.130
and re-emergence of a completely retooled
Barton.

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:49.060
After all, the man really just wants to be
with his family, right?

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:52.780
Not only would a time jump give him space
to train in the ways of the samurai, the loss

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:57.080
of his loved ones could also turn him into
a lawless badass with nothing to lose, back

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:59.269
in action as an Avenger-but-for-real-now.

00:03:59.269 --> 00:04:03.269
If this is how it happens, he'd need a little
time to develop that new persona.

00:04:03.269 --> 00:04:05.940
If the five-year rumor is true… the timeline
could fit.

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:09.400
To us, this time-jump rumor is pretty compelling.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:12.379
But there's one aspect about the theory that
gives us pause.

00:04:12.379 --> 00:04:17.139
One thing Infinity War lacked during its two-and-a-half
hour runtime was a proper reunion between

00:04:17.139 --> 00:04:19.069
Steve Rogers and Tony Stark.

00:04:19.069 --> 00:04:22.580
The last time the two were in the same room,
they were more or less trying to murder each

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:23.580
other.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:25.490
And that was way back in 2016.

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:29.789
By the time Infinity War rolled around, Stark
was still reluctant to pick up the phone and

00:04:29.789 --> 00:04:31.770
make the call to his "friend from work."

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:35.610
By the end of the movie, they've both lost
and they still haven't reunited.

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:39.900
The problem with a five-year time jump is
simple audiences want to see Steve and Tony

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:40.900
hug it out.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:45.330
Would they really skip such an anticipated
reunion by starting the movie in the future?

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:48.949
Or would the two somehow still be avoiding
each other, five years later?

00:04:48.949 --> 00:04:53.050
You can't jump that far into the future and
tell us Captain America and Iron Man haven't

00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:54.360
made up yet …can you?

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.689
It's like, grow up, guys, the world is ruined.

00:04:56.689 --> 00:04:58.219
Have a beer and talk it out.

00:04:58.219 --> 00:05:02.270
It is possible that the two heroes could avoid
each other for five whole years.

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:06.880
Or maybe the movie skips ahead five years
after Tony returns to Earth, and Tony and

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:08.219
Cap have regrouped.

00:05:08.219 --> 00:05:10.879
One way or another, audiences need that scene.

00:05:10.879 --> 00:05:13.189
Would a time jump really deny it to us?

00:05:13.189 --> 00:05:14.189
Maybe.

00:05:14.189 --> 00:05:17.600
But knowing these movies, it might end up
being worth it no matter how things actually

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:18.600
go down.

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:21.580
We'll see what happens when Avengers 4 lands
in 2019.

